useEffect handles side effects:
```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

function DataFetcher() {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  // Fetch data on component mount
  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('https://api.example.com/data')
      .then(response => response.json())
      .then(data => {
        setData(data);
        setLoading(false);
      });
  }, []); // Empty dependency array = run once on mount

  // Update document title when data changes
  useEffect(() => {
    if (data) {
      document.title = `Data loaded: ${data.length} items`;
    }
  }, [data]); // Run when data changes

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  return <div>Data: {JSON.stringify(data)}</div>;
}
```

Indexing improves query performance:
```sql
-- Basic indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_customer_email ON Customers(email);
CREATE INDEX idx_order_date ON Orders(order_date);

-- Composite index (multiple columns)
CREATE INDEX idx_name_department ON Employees(last_name, department_id);

-- Unique index
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_unique_username ON Users(username);

-- Partial index (only part of the data)
CREATE INDEX idx_active_users ON Users(id) WHERE is_active = true;

-- Considerations:
-- 1. Indexes speed up SELECT but slow down INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE
-- 2. Choose columns frequently used in WHERE, JOIN, ORDER BY
-- 3. Monitor index usage and maintenance
-- 4. Consider covering indexes for common queries

-- Example covering index:
CREATE INDEX idx_customer_covering ON Customers(
  last_name, 
  first_name
) INCLUDE (email, phone);
```

